----------------------------------------------------
- How Can We Insert and Remove ArrayList Elements? -
----------------------------------------------------

Inserting and removing elements of an ArrayList is much easier than the equivalent operations for an array. This is because 
the ArrayList class defines methods to perform each of these operations, and the ArrayList will automatically adjust its size.

---------------------------------------------------
	Inserting Elements
---------------------------------------------------

To insert an element into an ArrayList, we can use an overloaded version of the add method. One version of the add method (which we have already discussed) takes a single argument and appends an element with that argument's value to the end of 
the list. There is an overloaded version of the add method which takes two arguments - the first argument is an int index at 
which the second argument value is to be inserted.

** Use the overloaded add method - To insert an element into an ArrayList. **

if you had a element ArrayList with names in it.
names.add(1, "Batman"); -> will add this to the index of 1 and makes the list 3 to 4 elements.

-----------------------------------------------------
	Removing Elements
----------------------------------------------------

** Use the remove method - To remove an element from an ArrayList. **

take the same list and you can make a remove element in the same list like
names.remove(1);
